// Solution root: owns no files and references the two tier projects. The
// editor (tsserver) follows `references` to open each file under the tier
// that owns it. `npm run typecheck` (`tsc -b`) also checks a shared-pure
// module a Node module imports under the Node tier, which the editor does
// not. A file in no tier gets tsserver's non-strict inferred project. The
// tiers stay non-composite: viz's tiers import across
// each other on purpose, which composite projects reject (TS6307).
// src/sharedPure.test.ts fails if a viz source file is in neither tier
// project or in both. See FE-142.
{
  "files": [],
  "references": [
    { "path": "./tsconfig.browser.json" },
    { "path": "./tsconfig.node.json" }
  ]
}
